  "notes": "Official JBU plans index (catoid=33, Undergraduate Catalog 2025-2026). Transcribed 2026-10-01 from the official PDF. 'Bachelor of Science in Mechanical Engineering (BSME) — Class of 2029 (2025-2026 Catalog)', Revised 3/20/25; stamped catalog_year 2025-2026 honestly. The source is a prerequisite flowchart that prints course codes and term-hour headers but no per-course credit values. Credit hours follow JBU's official published course-numbering rule (JBU Course Descriptions, Undergraduate Catalog 2025-2026, catalog.jbu.edu): 'Course offerings are numbered utilizing four digits, the first indicating college year and the last the number of semester hours credit.' Paired lecture/lab boxes are sequenced as one flowchart box at combined hours (e.g. CHM 1123/1121 = 3+1 = 4); spot-verified against catalog course descriptions (EN 4343 Engineering Economics 'Three hours'; EN 4113/EN 4123 Capstone I/II 'Three hours'; ME 2562 Engineering Materials Science 'Two hours'; ME 2561 Engineering Materials Science Lab 'One hour'; EN 1322 Concepts in Electrical Engineering 'Two hours'; ME 2222 Thermodynamics 'Two hours'; ME 2453 Engineering Statics 'Three hours'). Term placement was re-verified 2026-10-01 by PDF text-geometry analysis (each course box mapped to its term column by x-coordinate against the eight printed term headers); all eight sequenced term sums match the printed term-hour headers exactly (14/15/16/16/15/17/15/16), total 124. Course titles are transcribed exactly as abbreviated on the flowchart boxes. The 'Engineering Practicums' (EN 1121 Production Techniques Laboratory, EN 1141 Introduction to CNC Machining, EN 1151 Introduction to PLCs) are printed 'Recommended but not required' and are excluded from the sequenced hours. Annotations preserved: 'CS 1113: also offered Summer B'; solid arrows = prerequisites, dashed arrows = corequisites. Dashed-box note preserved: 'These courses can be taken senior year as necessary to make room for technical elective(s)' (BBL 2013, EN 3513). 2026-10-01 audit: corrected term misassignments (BBL 1023, BBL 2013, EN 3513 were in wrong terms).",
